            ],
            "correct_choice_labels": [
              "A"
            ],
            "correct_answer": "The support is $[4,20]$ and the peak amplitude stays $7$.",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "The factor inside the argument is $\\tfrac{1}{2}$, so write the signal as $x(at)$ with $a=\\tfrac{1}{2}$. For time expansion, each original time point moves to $t_{new}=t_0/a$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "a=\\tfrac{1}{2},\\qquad t_{new}=t_0/a=2t_0",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "So the endpoints $2$ and $10$ move to $4$ and $20$. The support expands away from $t=0$, and the amplitudes do not change.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
